PolkaVM App v2 browser runtime
Source repository: https://github.com/paritytech/host-rust-core
Source commit: 92e4e4f27ea328e4326e7a5e11987b648228a49f
Source branch: https://github.com/paritytech/host-rust-core/tree/feat/pvm-app-runtime
Package: js/packages/pvm-browser-runtime

Vendored package artifacts:
- pvm-browser-runtime.wasm
- pvm-gpu-worker.js
- pvm-wasm-worker.js

Rebuild from the pinned source with:
  npm --prefix js/packages/pvm-browser-runtime run build

The package build compiles the host-neutral Rust runtime, bundles the translator
and worker entry for opaque sandbox workers, and emits SHA-256 checksums. The
worker reports translation, compilation, startup, and update timing metrics and
returns translated Wasm bytes for the sandbox's digest-keyed IndexedDB cache.
The runtime implements the bounded framebuffer, Tri2D, and WebGPU Raster
profiles while retaining the interpreter as a guarded fallback.
